,2006]]},"yurai":{"25":{"大津市":"After the Ōmi-Ōtsu palace was abandoned the place was called Furutsu, 'the old capital's harbour'; with the move to Heian-kyō in 794 it revived as Ōtsu, the new capital's port.","長浜市":"Originally Imahama; Hashiba (Toyotomi) Hideyoshi renamed it Nagahama around 1575. Some say the \"naga\" honours his lord Oda Nobunaga, but there is no proof.","彦根市":"Ikutsuhikone, a child of the sun goddess Amaterasu, was enshrined on Mount Hikone — the lakeside hill where Hikone Castle was later built.","甲賀市":"The reading \"Kōka\" is traced to the Kafuka (鹿深) clan of Baekje descent who ruled here in ancient times. Public facilities say \"Kōka\", but surnames and businesses often say \"Kōga\".","守山市":"Either Tōmon-in, a temple that \"guarded\" (mori) Mount Hiei across Lake Biwa, or the keepers (yamamori) of nearby Mount Tsuga.","近江八幡市":"Named after Himure Hachiman Shrine. Fukuoka already had a Yahata City in 1954, so the new city added the province name Ōmi. Fukuoka's Yahata later merged into Kitakyūshū, and when Kyoto's Yawata became a city in 1977 no prefix was needed — so the older city carries one and the newer does not."}},"kyu":{"25201":{"t":140,"k":58742,"r":[["Zeze Domain",21377],["@bakufu",13353],["@jisha",12490],["Sano Domain",6410],["@other",5112]]},"25202":{"t":111,"k":62405,"r":[["Hikone Domain",50546],["@bakufu",11715],["@jisha",144]]},"25203":{"t":282,"k":156092,"r":[["Hikone Domain",61112],["@bakufu",39371],["Kōriyama Domain",12195],["Yodo Domain",10837],["@other",32577]]},"25204":{"t":101,"k":58913,"r":[["@bakufu",17255],["@hatamoto",13734],["Kōriyama Domain",12643],["Kawagoe Domain",5922],["@other",9359]]},"25206":{"t":42,"k":29091,"r":[["Zeze Domain",17395],["@hatamoto",4113],["@bakufu",3229],["Yodo Domain",1354],["@other",3000]]},"25207":{"t":53,"k":35109,"r":[["@hatamoto",10787],["Yodo Domain",5736],["@bakufu",5493],["Miyazu Domain",3386],["@other",9707]]},"25208":{"t":40,"k":21795,"r":[["Zeze Domain",6294],["@hatamoto",6260],["@baku